### Goal Model Summary

Below is the structured goal model based on the mission description, decomposed into goals and tasks with their respective relationships and properties.

---

### Goals Table

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition**/**Enquired Information** | **Relation** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------|--------------|
| **G1** | Manage food and dish delivery and retrieval in the hospital | - | Achieve | All food deliveries and dish retrievals are successfully completed | - |
| **G2** | Deliver food from the kitchen to an inpatient room | - | Perform | Food is successfully delivered to the inpatient room | AND |
| **G3** | Retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room | - | Perform | Dirty dishes are successfully retrieved from the inpatient room | AND |
| **G2.1** | Retrieve food from the kitchen | - | Perform | Food is successfully retrieved from the kitchen | AND |
| **G2.2** | Deliver food directly to the room table | - | Perform | Food is successfully placed on the room table | AND |
| **G2.3** | Deliver food via robot tray | - | Perform | Food is successfully placed on the robot tray | AND |
| **G2.3.1** | Indicate the correct meal to the inpatient | - | Perform | Correct meal is indicated to the inpatient | AND |
| **G2.3.2** | Track meal retrieval | - | Perform | Meal retrieval is successfully tracked | AND |
| **G2.3.3** | Alert if wrong meal is retrieved | - | Perform | Alert is issued if wrong meal is retrieved | AND |
| **G3.1** | Retrieve dishes unassisted | - | Perform | Dishes are successfully retrieved unassisted | AND |
| **G3.2** | Retrieve dishes with cooperation | - | Perform | Dishes are successfully retrieved with cooperation | AND |
| **G3.2.1** | Call for help if needed | - | Perform | Help is successfully requested if needed | AND |

---

### Tasks Table

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|-----------------------|
| **AT1** | Retrieve food from the kitchen | AND | Kitchen | 1 |
| **AT2** | Deliver food to the room table | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT3** | Deliver food via robot tray | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT4** | Indicate the correct meal | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT5** | Track meal retrieval | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT6** | Alert if wrong meal is retrieved | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT7** | Retrieve dishes unassisted | AND | Patient's room | 1 |
| **AT8** | Retrieve dishes with cooperation | AND | Patient's room | 1 or more |
| **AT9** | Call for help if needed | AND | Patient's room | 1 |

---

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND]**
- **G2.3 -> G2.3.1, G2.3.2, G2.3.3 [AND]**
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND]**
- **G3.2 -> G3.2.1 [AND]**

---

This model ensures that the system can handle both food delivery and dish retrieval efficiently, considering various scenarios and cooperation possibilities.
